 ## Overview
-This method ensures the integrity of input tensors before invoking the CUDA rasterization backend by validating mutually exclusive representations for color and 3D covariance. It standardizes missing inputs into empty tensors of appropriate shapes, preventing runtime errors in the differentiable rendering loop. It differs from [GaussianRasterizationSettings](2924-gaussianrasterizationsettings.md) by handling data structure normalization rather than just configuration storage, and from the [Gaussian Splatting Rendering Pipeline](3415-gaussian-splatting-rendering-pipeline.md) by focusing strictly on pre-rasterization input consistency rather than the full execution flow.
+The `GaussianRasterizer` initialization and input validation phase ensures that the data structures passed to the CUDA rasterization backend are consistent, mutually exclusive where required, and device-compatible before kernel execution. It solves the problem of ambiguous or malformed input configurations that would cause undefined behavior or runtime errors in the differentiable rendering pipeline. It is distinguished from the broader [Gaussian Splatting Rendering Pipeline](3415-gaussian-splatting-rendering-pipeline.md) by focusing strictly on pre-kernel data integrity checks and tensor preparation rather than the actual rasterization logic.
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-- `means3D`: Tensor of shape $(N, 3)$, Gaussian centers.
-- `shs`: Tensor of Spherical Harmonics coefficients, shape $(N, K, C)$ or $(N, C)$ depending on implementation.
-- `colors_precomp`: Tensor of pre-computed RGB values, shape $(N, 3)$.
-- `scales`: Tensor of scale factors, shape $(N, 3)$.
-- `rotations`: Tensor of quaternion rotations, shape $(N, 4)$.
-- `cov3D_precomp`: Tensor of pre-computed 3D covariances, shape $(N, 6)$ or $(N, 3, 3)$.
-- `features`: Optional tensor of additional features.
-- `raster_settings`: Configuration object containing camera intrinsics, extrinsics, and rasterization flags.
+- `raster_settings`: An instance of `GaussianRasterizationSettings` containing camera intrinsics, extrinsics, and rasterization flags.
+- `means3D`: Tensor of shape `(N, 3)` representing 3D Gaussian centers.
+- `shs`: Tensor of shape `(N, K, C)` for Spherical Harmonics coefficients, or `None`.
+- `colors_precomp`: Tensor of shape `(N, 3)` for pre-computed RGB colors, or `None`.
+- `scales`: Tensor of shape `(N, 3)` for parametric scales, or `None`.
+- `rotations`: Tensor of shape `(N, 4)` for parametric rotations (quaternions), or `None`.
+- `cov3D_precomp`: Tensor of shape `(N, 6)` for pre-computed 3D covariances, or `None`.
